 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`code/TauCeti/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/PiL2.lean` already holds Tau Ceti's `EuclideanSpace` linear-isometry API. The definition body is just `Fin.snoc` with `WithLp.toLp`/`ofLp`. The same zero-append is the stage map RP\u207f \u2192 RP\u207f\u207a\u00b9 (`\ud835\udd5c = \u211d`), which the C1.5 target also covers.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/ComplexProjectiveSpace/Inclusion.lean",
   "fix": "Move it to `TauCeti/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/PiL2.lean` (or a similar Euclidean-space file), generalised to any `RCLike \ud835\udd5c`, with a name such as `EuclideanSpace.snocZero`, and keep its simp lemmas there.",
   "issue": "`ComplexProjectiveSpace.appendZero` (plus `appendZero_apply_castSucc`, `appendZero_apply_last`, `appendZero_init`) is a linear isometry `EuclideanSpace \ud835\udd5c (Fin (n+1)) \u2192\u2097\u1d62 EuclideanSpace \ud835\udd5c (Fin (n+2))` whose statements mention only Mathlib types and do not depend on CP\u207f. Filing it under the `ComplexProjectiveSpace` namespace hides it from anyone who needs it for the RP\u207f stage maps.",
   "line": 46
  },
  {
   "evidence": "In the diff, `theorem inclusion_mk` has no attribute, and `inclusion_injective` and `mk_mem_range_inclusion_iff` both begin with `rw [inclusion_mk ...]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/ComplexProjectiveSpace/Inclusion.lean",
   "fix": "Tag `inclusion_mk` `@[simp]`.",
   "issue": "`inclusion_mk` is the lemma that computes `inclusion` on classes `mk n x`, and it is not tagged `@[simp]`. Because `inclusion`'s body is hidden, `simp` cannot evaluate `inclusion n (mk n x)` and callers must rewrite with this lemma by hand; the PR's own proofs do this (`rw [inclusion_mk, inclusion_mk, ...]`).",
   "line": 100
  }
 ],
